                <pb facs="0307" n="299" xml:id="pg299"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15776: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-22T18:00:00+09:00">March 22, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 22—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. According to the <hi rendition="#italic">Asahi</hi>, the Minister of War
                    made the following reply to an interpellation in the Budget Committee of the
                    Lower House this morning regarding the attitude of the fighting services toward
                    the Nine Power Pact: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“With respect to the Nine Power Pact, the army will of course conform to
                            the Government’s policy. As for my private opinion, however, the present
                            China incident was brought about by the anti-Japanese policy of the
                            Chiang regime, and is literally a holy war for the purpose of correcting
                            this mistaken policy and of ensuring the lasting peace of East Asia.
                            Consequently, the present incident in my opinion transcends the Nine
                            Power Pact. While the said instrument still exists, Japan will not be
                            restricted by it in its military operations. It goes without saying that
                            the present situation in East Asia generally is far different from the
                            time when the Nine Power Pact was concluded.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Air mail to Shanghai and Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
